{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'func IsAdministrativePath|module-metadata' pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_material*; sed -n '110,180p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_material.go; cat pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md | head -65; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | tail -36; sed -n '663,738p' pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go; sed -n '236,250p' .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\"","aggregated_output":"rg: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_material*: IO error for operation on pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_material*: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsed: can't read pose-mcp/internal/pose/delivery_material.go: No such file or directory\n# Adversarial corpus\n\nSpec: `pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus`. Test: `adversarial_corpus_test.go`.\n\nEvery gate POSE adds against mechanical compliance can itself be satisfied\nmechanically. Each row is the cheapest formal satisfaction of one gate. An\n`enforced` case fails the build when the shortcut works again; a `known-gap`\ncase fails the build when the gap closes, so it cannot close or reopen\nsilently; a `planned` case belongs to a spec not yet delivered and gains code\nbefore that spec closes; a `delegated` case is enforced by a test in another\npackage, named in the row, whose existence the corpus checks.\n\nThis corpus belongs to developing POSE's governance. It adds no checklist to an\nadopting project's features.\n\n| Case | Status | Shortcut it refuses | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `human-label-without-confirmation` | enforced | An agent writes and applies a review under `human:<name>`; the record reads as a human review | pose-review-attribution-roles |\n| `declared-independent-prefix` | enforced | `agent:independent-*` under declared assurance reads as authenticated separation | pose-review-assurance-disclosure |\n| `confirmation-reused-for-edited-content` | enforced | A confirmation recorded for one set of conclusions is kept after they change | pose-review-attribution-roles |\n| `unknown-recorded-as-satisfied` | enforced | An obligation the engine could not observe is reported as satisfied | pose-obligation-contract |\n| `legacy-blocker-gains-an-actor` | enforced | A blocker known only as text is given an invented recipient | pose-obligation-contract |\n| `blocked-counted-as-resolved` | enforced | Operational waiting counts as a resolved outcome in success metrics | pose-blocked-semantics-alignment |\n| `flat-specs-share-one-journal` | enforced | Two flat specs record amendments in one shared journal | pose-flat-spec-amendments |\n| `local-metadata-read-as-published` | enforced | A locally read version is presented as a proven publication | pose-public-claims-publication-provenance |\n| `invented-trace-test-ref` | known-gap | A requirement trace cites a test that does not exist and `lint-spec --strict` passes (follow-up 097 of pose-abm-design-basis) | pose-mechanization-adversarial-corpus |\n| `unavailable-producer-reads-as-empty` | enforced | A producer fails and Attention reports zero obligations as a complete answer | pose-obligation-projection |\n| `trivial-change-raises-a-request` | enforced | A trivial change or an already-authorized instruction produces an ActionRequest | pose-action-requests |\n| `declined-approval-satisfies` | enforced | A declined approval, or a cancellation without authority, releases a gate | pose-action-request-resolution |\n| `closeout-plan-fills-judgment` | enforced | The recoverable closeout plan answers a judgment criterion to finish | pose-recoverable-closeout-plan |\n| `ready-from-absent-blockers` | enforced | Absence of a known blocker is presented as proven independence | pose-phase-scoped-readiness |\n| `stale-preview-authorizes-apply` | enforced | A start previewed before a restricting request is applied after it | pose-governed-effect-enforcement |\n| `code-change-keeps-judgment` | enforced | The reviewed code changes and every criterion still reads as equivalent, so the old judgment is reused | pose-material-equivalence-reuse |\n| `minimal-surface-skips-trace` | enforced | A done spec declares the minimal surface to drop its requirement trace | pose-progressive-spec-surface |\n| `stale-assessment-reused` | enforced | The assessed component changes and the old assessment still reads as fresh | pose-adaptive-assessment-freshness |\n| `unpinned-premise-trigger-reads-current` | enforced | A premise trigger without a pin can never go stale and nothing says so | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n| `calendar-ttl-as-premise-trigger` | enforced | An arbitrary expiry date is accepted as the material trigger of a premise | pose-assumption-validity-scope |\n| `unobserved-falsifier-reads-uncontradicted` | enforced | An unbound legacy index cannot prove that a falsifier check was never observed | pose-falsifier-reconsideration |\n| `parity-row-cites-an-unrelated-test` | known-gap | A launcher parity row names a real but unrelated `pose delegate` command and an existing test that does not exercise the capability, and the parity check passes; the check proves existence, review of the cited tests proves coverage | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `imported-fragment-completes-a-replaced-command` | known-gap | A usage or error string assembles a removed command from a constant of another package of the module, which the active-document check reads as a gap; review of assembled messages is the defence | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `cgo-preamble-text-reaches-usage` | known-gap | Operator text written as a C string in a cgo preamble reaches a usage surface; the Go reader sees a comment, not a string | pose-delegation-parity-gate |\n| `later-removal-hides-a-later-touch` | delegated | A later removal satisfies an earlier spec's claim because the history it is judged on omits that spec's change after the removal — change sets in ID order, a merge, root or type-change touch, a failed or shallow read, a recorded report too wide to read whole or a history directory that cannot be listed, a replace ref or graft (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_gaps_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundTwo`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundThree`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundFive`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `rename-read-as-removal` | delegated | A rename, or a path spelled as a pathspec, is taken for the declared deletion (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `recorded-commit-is-an-option` | delegated | A change set read from a recorded report names a Git option or a tag where a commit belongs (`cli/delivery_later_removal_history_test.go:TestLaterRemovalHistoryShapes`, `cli/delivery_later_removal_raw_test.go:TestLaterRemovalReviewRoundThree`) | pose-delivery-later-removal |\n| `peer-removal-stands-for-a-member` | delegated | A review subject digests a removed path from a peer's accepted removal while another observing member — sorted later, sharing a commit, or reduced into the peer's set — has none, whatever action or rename it observed the path with (`pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestReviewSubjectReadsALaterRemovalFromItsWitness`, `pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestMilestoneSubjectRemovalHoldsForEveryMember`) | pose-review-subject-later-removal |\n| `retained-child-skips-its-verification` | delegated | A milestone seals over a done member whose own review verification no longer retains its approval — revoked federated trust, lost history, a later negative review (`pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestRetainedChildFollowsItsVerification`, `pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestMilestoneSealRetainsADoneChildsApprovedReview`) | pose-review-subject-later-removal |\n| `run-pattern-names-no-test` | delegated | A validation check's `-run` alternative names a test that no longer exists, or never did, and the check passes on Go's exit 0 — through `-run=`, a build-excluded or ignored file, a vendored or nested-module declaration, a benchmark or a name Go does not run (`cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestDeadRunPatternGuardFollowsGoSelection`, `cli/validation_matrix_patterns_test.go:TestValidationMatrixRunPatternsNameExistingTests`); a non-plain pattern passes only when listed with its reason | pose-validation-matrix-dead-test-patterns |\n| `removal-witness-outlives-its-history` | delegated | A stale index keeps counting a removal after a later touch, through a merge, a rewritten history or a shallow clone that lost the touch (`pose/removal_witness_freshness_test.go:TestLaterTouchRefusesTheWitness`, `pose/removal_witness_freshness_test.go:TestShallowHistoryRefusesTheWitness`) | pose-removal-witness-freshness |\n| `parent-outlives-a-rejected-child` | delegated | A milestone or roadmap stays approved over a child's later rejection, through retention, a sealed cycle, a replaced approval or a forged `replaces` (`pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestParentApprovalFollowsAChildsRejection`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestChildCycleEndsInARefusal`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestForgedReplacementRetiresNothing`, `pose/review_approval_follows_children_test.go:TestLegacyCoordinatedMatchingFollowsLineage`) | pose-review-approval-follows-children |\n| `go-check-ran-no-test` | delegated | A `go test` check selects nothing and passes on Go's exit 0, through a flag spelling, a flag's value read as a flag, or a package without test files (`cli/validate_empty_go_checks_test.go:TestValidateRefusesAGoCheckThatRanNoTest`, `cli/validate_empty_go_checks_test.go:TestGoTestSelection`); a check outside the plain grammar passes unjudged, and a test printing a result line can still mislead it | pose-validate-refuses-empty-go-checks |\n| `request-opened-after-preview-transfers` | delegated | A request opened after a transfer preview is moved with the spec (`pose/spec_transfer_actions_test.go:TestTransferRefusesARequestOpenedAfterThePreview`) | pose-transfer-preserves-obligations |\n\n| `deleted-reservation-resets-quota` | delegated | Deleting a reservation and receipt makes a surviving run stop consuming quota | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `witness-bundle-filter-hides-loss` | delegated | Editing a witness bundle makes scoped readers skip its corruption | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `window-erases-rerun` | delegated | Moving a prior run outside the time window turns a rerun into a first attempt | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n| `canned-executor-approval-proves-cognition` | delegated | A complete canned approval from a trusted local command is presented as proof of review cognition or a vendor receipt (`cli/delegated_review_capability_test.go:TestDelegatedReviewCapabilityCannedApprovalDisclosesItsLimits` guards disclosure; the engine cannot detect canned judgments) | pose-delegated-review-capability |\n| `oversized-writer-publishes-unreadable-run` | delegated | A writer reports completion for a run its bounded reader immediately refuses | pose-delegated-review-attempt-ledger |\n   617\t\treturn true\n   618\t}\n   619\t\n   620\t// headReflogLength counts the entries of HEAD's reflog; -1 when it cannot be\n   621\t// read or reflogs are disabled.\n   622\tfunc headReflogLength(root string) int {\n   623\t\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"reflog\", \"show\", \"--format=%H\", \"HEAD\", \"--\").Output()\n   624\t\tif err != nil {\n   625\t\t\treturn -1\n   626\t\t}\n   627\t\tlines := strings.Count(string(out), \"\\n\")\n   628\t\tif lines == 0 {\n   629\t\t\treturn -1\n   630\t\t}\n   631\t\treturn lines\n   632\t}\n   633\t\n   634\t// submodulesCheckedOut returns a gitlink of head whose working repository is\n   635\t// missing or not at the recorded commit; \"\" when every one is.\n   636\tfunc submodulesCheckedOut(root, head string) string {\n   637\t\tlinks, err := gitlinks(root, head)\n   638\t\tif err != nil {\n   639\t\t\treturn \"(gitlinks unreadable)\"\n   640\t\t}\n   641\t\tfor sub, commit := range links {\n   642\t\t\trepo := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(sub))\n   643\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(repo, \".git\")); err != nil {\n   644\t\t\t\treturn sub\n   645\t\t\t}\n   646\t\t\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", repo, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").Output()\n   647\t\t\tif err != nil || strings.TrimSpace(string(out)) != commit {\n   648\t\t\t\treturn sub\n   649\t\t\t}\n   650\t\t}\n   651\t\treturn \"\"\n   652\t}\n\tclean := filepath.Clean(filepath.FromSlash(path))\n\treturn !filepath.IsAbs(clean) && clean != \"..\" && !strings.HasPrefix(clean, \"..\"+string(filepath.Separator))\n}\n\nfunc discoverValidationModulesIn(files posemodel.Files, root string) ([]validationModule, error) {\n\t// testdata/fixture(s): see index.go's scanModules for why these are\n\t// excluded (spec pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes).\n\tignored := map[string]bool{\".git\": true, \".qwen\": true, \"node_modules\": true, \"vendor\": true, \".venv\": true, \".pnpm-store\": true, \"target\": true, \"dist\": true, \"build\": true, \".next\": true, \"coverage\": true, \".pose\": true, \"testdata\": true, \"fixture\": true, \"fixtures\": true}\n\t// A gitignored subtree (a locally-checked-out project the repository\n\t// deliberately excludes, e.g. a vendored tool) is never a governed\n\t// deliverable module — see posemodel.GitIgnoredPaths (spec\n\t// pose-discovery-gitignore-and-root-alias-fix).\n\tgitIgnored := posemodel.GitIgnoredPathsIn(files, root)\n\tbyPath := map[string]string{}\n\terr := posemodel.WalkDirIn(files, root, func(path string, entry os.DirEntry, err error) error {\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif entry.IsDir() {\n\t\t\tif path != root && ignored[entry.Name()] {\n\t\t\t\treturn filepath.SkipDir\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif path != root {\n\t\t\t\tif rel, relErr := filepath.Rel(root, path); relErr == nil && (gitIgnored[filepath.ToSlash(rel)+\"/\"] || gitIgnored[filepath.ToSlash(rel)]) {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn filepath.SkipDir\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\t// spec pose-stack-catalog-expansion: the Python manager (poetry/\n\t\t// pipenv/pip/setuptools/pep517) is resolved by the matrix `when`\n\t\t// predicates, not at discovery time — every marker maps to the\n\t\t// \"python\" stack. stackForManifestFile is shared with scanModules\n\t\t// (spec pose-validation-scanner-consolidation) so a stack-detection\n\t\t// fix here applies there too.\n\t\tstack := stackForManifestFile(entry.Name())\n\t\tif stack != \"\" {\n\t\t\t// Existing overwrite-by-walk-order semantics preserved\n\t\t\t// unchanged for compatibility; `pose stacks` surfaces the full\n\t\t\t// per-directory catalog resolution (including any conflicting\n\t\t\t// markers) independently of what this single-stack map picks.\n\t\t\tbyPath[filepath.Dir(path)] = stack\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tmodules := make([]validationModule, 0, len(byPath))\n\tfor abs, stack := range byPath {\n\t\tif stack == \"java\" && isAndroidModuleIn(files, abs) {\n\t\t\t// A Gradle module carrying an AndroidManifest.xml is an Android\n\t\t\t// app/library, not a generic JVM backend module — conflating the\n\t\t\t// two under \"java\" made every Android module's domain\n\t\t\t// misleading (spec pose-upgrade-path-audit-fixes). Kotlin-only\n\t\t\t// non-Android Gradle modules are unaffected: they have no\n\t\t\t// AndroidManifest.xml and keep classifying as \"java\".\n\t\t\tstack = \"android\"\n\t\t}\n\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(root, abs)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tmodules = append(modules, validationModule{filepath.ToSlash(rel), abs, stack})\n\t}\n\tsort.Slice(modules, func(i, j int) bool { return modules[i].Rel < modules[j].Rel })\n\treturn modules, nil\n}\n\n// discoverValidationModules reads and writes the filesystem directly; discoverValidationModulesIn takes the\n// operation's files.\nfunc discoverValidationModules(root string) ([]validationModule, error) {\n\treturn discoverValidationModulesIn(posemodel.NativeFiles(), root)\n}\n\n// isAndroidModule reports whether a Gradle module directory is an Android\n`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n\n### Validation executed\nSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n\n### Residual risks\nAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n\n### Follow-ups\n- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
