{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nTwo high-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **N40 — incomplete start-state checks**, `validate.go:1447`: full runs check submodule initialization and hidden index flags only at the end. A check can pass against absent or hidden material, restore the committed state, and produce a reusable `material_clean` record.\n- **N41 — cleanliness sampled after planning**, `validate.go:1158`: uncommitted manifests can influence module discovery and be restored before `startedClean` is sampled, without moving HEAD.\n- **N42 — low follow-up**, `validate.go:1616`: reports still present carried checks as executed commands without their original head and time. This remains tracked as F2.\n\nThese blockers are source-traced; new synthetic reproductions were unavailable because scratch-directory creation was denied. Existing focused tests, race tests, delivery-parser tests, publication-guard tests and `go vet` passed. The full validation reruns were invoked but had not completed at conclusion; their tool dispositions below cite the supplied sealed canonical evidence.\n\nApplied the review workflow and security, backend-Go, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. The checkout remained unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N40\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1447,\n      \"summary\": \"Full-run cleanliness establishes submodule checkout and hidden-index conditions only at the end. startedClean at line 1158 calls materialWorktreeClean, which does not reject uninitialized submodules or hidden index entries. For example, start with an uninitialized b/data whose recorded commit contains fail; a b check can pass test ! -f data/fail, then initialize the submodule before returning successfully. The final checkout, status, parent HEAD and reflog all satisfy the current calculation, so material_clean becomes true and a subsequent unchanged carry can reuse a pass that would now fail. Likewise, a check can pass against a skip-worktree-hidden local fix, restore the committed failing file and clear the flag before the final hiddenIndexEntries call. Validate these conditions before planning/execution as well as at completion, retaining a failed initial condition. This violates R2 and D1. Established by source trace; the existing uninitialized-submodule test covers only a submodule that remains uninitialized.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N41\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1158,\n      \"summary\": \"startedClean is sampled after reading the matrix at line 1048 and discovering modules at line 1076. Pinning HEAD and its reflog does not establish that these working-copy inputs matched that commit. A temporarily modified or removed manifest can cause discovery to choose the wrong stack or omit a module, then be restored before line 1158. HEAD and its reflog need never move; the run can execute the stale plan and publish material_clean=true with available material bindings. Establish cleanliness before consuming plan inputs and bind or revalidate those inputs against the pinned snapshot. This violates R2 and the clean-material premise of D1. Established by source trace; no new concurrent fixture was executed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N42\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1616,\n      \"summary\": \"Existing F2 remains: validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in Commands and renders their old outcome and duration without carried_from or carried_generated_at. A newly dated --report therefore presents reused checks as commands executed by this run. Source trace: lines 1612-1629; the owned follow-up is recorded at spec line 246.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F2: exclude carried checks from executed commands and label reused results with their original head and generation time.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N36\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1713 and :1746 force core.fileMode=true for both cleanliness status reads. TestValidateModeChangeHiddenByConfigurationIsNotClean passed in the focused CLI test run, including the race-detector run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N37\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1042-1046 now samples HEAD and its reflog before the matrix read at :1048 and module discovery at :1076, closing the reported concurrent-checkout ordering route. N41 separately identifies working-copy plan inputs that need not match that pinned commit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N38\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1447-1448 now rejects a submodule still uninitialized at completion; TestValidateUninitializedSubmoduleIsNotClean passed. No equivalent initial check is retained for full runs, leaving the initialize-during-run route described in N40.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1612-1629 still omits carry provenance and includes carried commands. Spec line 246 records owned follow-up F2. N42 retains this as a low follow-up with action, owner and review date.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R10 and D1-D3, the ADR, all implementation changes, regression fixtures, help and English/pt-BR manuals with scaffold copies. Swept eligibility and fallback, matrix/engine identity, administrative exclusions, cancellation, missing/duplicate base results, outcomes and counts, chained provenance, delivery parsing, changed-path ownership, dependencies, nested/root modules, manifestless overrides, criticality widening, gitlinks/submodules, symlinks, case/ASCII restrictions, hidden index flags, mode changes, HEAD/reflog ordering, start/end cleanliness, and guarded atomic canonical publication. Ran focused CLI/pose tests, focused CLI race tests, delivery carried-head parsing, canonical-publication guard tests, go vet, artifact-check, design assessment, suggest-review and recurrence-check; recurrence reported zero flagged keys. Full root/module validation reruns were invoked but remained incomplete at conclusion; supplied sealed evidence is cited separately. Scratch creation was denied, preventing new reproductions and safely isolated persistent assessments. No carry-specific adversarial-corpus row was found; existing negative fixtures do not cover N40/N41. No repository edits or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The explicit selfContained declaration remains an accepted instance assumption. The stronger claim that a reusable base validated its committed material is not established at the beginning of full runs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N41\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected dispatcher lifecycle, silent carried entries, cancellation, publication guarding and planning order. Focused race tests passed, but they do not establish snapshot consistency during concurrent working-copy restoration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI flag and JSON fields are additive. Existing schema handling remains; legacy records without engine_version cannot supply carries. Delivery parsing preserves legacy run-level provenance and reads per-check carry provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected incompatible flags, missing canonical configuration, unsafe revisions, malformed metadata, base mismatch and conservative fallback paths. Focused negative fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Traced canonical publication and ParseDeliveryValidationRun into delivery results. The carried-head parser test passed independently. The spec explicitly retains the complete carried-bundle lifecycle test as follow-up F1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N42\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Structured records expose carry origin and fallback reasons, but the report projection loses that distinction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined argument handling, additive record fields and legacy delivery parsing. Existing records retain their interpretation; old records are conservatively ineligible as carry bases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing positive and negative fixtures passed, but the initial-material gap permits stale passes to become reusable clean bases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 correctly requires unchanged inputs before rebinding carried results to current material. Changed-scope selection and origin preservation address repeated full runs, but incomplete initial-state verification breaks that premise.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records the structural decision to reuse unchanged checks while preserving their actual origin, eligibility boundaries and the selfContained trade-off.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared CLI help, English and pt-BR manuals, embedded copies, spec and ADR. They describe the intended selection, eligibility, provenance and explicit declaration risk consistently. N40/N41 are implementation failures to establish those documented guarantees.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N42\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback explanations are actionable, while report readers cannot distinguish executed and reused checks. Existing owned F2 supplies the remediation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1 and R3-R10 have relevant implementation and regression coverage. R2 remains unsatisfied by the initial-state and planning gaps in N40/N41.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-13f5c227501b7382\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Changes remain within the approved CLI, selection, record, delivery-reader, help/manual and ADR scope. Inspected the artifact-check range expansion separately from the sealed implementation subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement, path/alias refusals and guarded publication preserve important boundaries, but the clean-base authority can still be granted to results obtained from absent or hidden material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-13f5c227501b7382\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module-level selection plus whole-matrix/engine invalidation is smaller than introducing arbitrary per-check input hashing and avoids speculative cache infrastructure. Manual result merging would lose provenance. The choice depends on correct module/dependency declarations and a verifiable clean base; inability to establish either requires a full run rather than wider reuse.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed with provenance warnings: 15 claims, 20 observed paths and 985 findings. Its trailer-derived range extends beyond the sealed implementation subject, consistent with the disclosed index-commit attribution issue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-13f5c227501b7382\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the JSON design assessment; it reported the ADR governance-contract delta and the sealed design digest.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d /tmp/pose-review-sweep.XXXXXX\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Persistent assessments require an isolated copy under the review boundary. Scratch creation failed with Read-only file system; the sealed checkout was not used for assessment